WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.831
Distinguish replication from decomposition.

00:00:02.831 --> 00:00:09.416
Replicas run the same application to serve more
requests; microservices divide responsibilities into

00:00:09.416 --> 00:00:11.589
separately deployable components.

00:00:11.589 --> 00:00:15.342
A monolith often simplifies development and
transactions.

00:00:15.342 --> 00:00:21.531
Its suitability depends on the system and team, so
begin with concrete change and coordination

00:00:21.531 --> 00:00:26.075
problems rather than assuming more services are
automatically better.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:30.492
Choose service boundaries around responsibilities
and change patterns.

00:00:30.492 --> 00:00:36.578
Network APIs hide implementation details, but calls
can fail independently and cross-service data

00:00:36.578 --> 00:00:38.837
updates require deliberate recovery.

00:00:38.837 --> 00:00:44.421
Compare the gain in independent deployment with the
added testing and operational burden.

00:00:44.421 --> 00:00:50.193
A service split is justified when those benefits
matter enough to pay the coordination cost.
